<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5333"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 7:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Im sure that this has been done and Id like to know the results...The box will have a production code on it indicating WHERE it was made, Im sure that from that it can be determined where and when it was shipped &#40;narrowing it down as to where it was purchased&#41;  <BR> <BR>The brick  could be analysied for the type of clay used and possibly where and when it was made &#40;Im guessing that that might not be possible due to the amount of clay present in that area&#41;. Same for the mortar, analysis of the sand used.  <BR> <BR>GOSH...if we only knew<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5333-->
<!--Post: 5382--><!--Time: 1107098423-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5382"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 7:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->the police could look for fingerprits, on the cereal box, from the person who put the ceral box on the shelf.  <BR>Then take fingerprints from all personel in Wichita stores who put that specific kind of cereal boxes &#40; I think that box was a special edition, maybe valentine because of the heart&#41; on their shelfs. <BR> <BR>Doing that they might be able to establish what store BTK bought the cereal box.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5382-->
<!--Post: 5397--><!--Time: 1107106376-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5397"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 9:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Since BTK is at least 1/2 mile ahead of everyone, I would not be surprised to see that the box is an old one, and I do mean old. He has the ability to plan years in advance, which has helped him avoid detection &#40;or at least apprehension&#41;. He may have dumpster-dived and gotten someone else&#39;s box with their fingerprints on it. Perhaps the Chief&#39;s cereal box. That would turn the tables, for sure. Sales of that cereal are sure to drop.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5397-->
<!--Post: 5402--><!--Time: 1107108025-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5402"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop- I believe that the cereal box, with the heart on it, is the newest style package. I recently bought a box of Post Grapenuts and it has the same picture, same design, of a heart.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5402-->
<!--Post: 5404--><!--Time: 1107109249-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5404"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK probably got it out of someones trash. Maybe even a convicted sex offender. Just to add a little interest to the situation. Their addresses are public Knowledge. The brick is surely just a standard brick, but it would be interesting if one was missing from WSU or another site w/ personalized bricks.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5404-->
<!--Post: 5408--><!--Time: 1107111185-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5408"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ksugirl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ksugirl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Essevi, you are correct about the heart graphic on Post brand cereal boxes.  My husband and I eat Post Raisin Bran, and the very same heart graphic appears on the boxes we purchase that appears on the BTK Toasties box.  Post markets these cereals as being &#34;heart healthy.&#34;  The BTK box is a recent one.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5408-->
<!--Post: 5410--><!--Time: 1107111500-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5410"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My husband grew up as a military brat in Germany and in the US. Interesting note: He said that kids that lived on base or &#34;post&#34; and were bus&#39;d in to public schools were called &#34;Post Toasties&#34; by the public school kids. Just a side note...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5410-->
<!--Post: 5440--><!--Time: 1107120570-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5440"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 1:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very interesting take on Post Toasties, Lilymarie, especially because of BTK&#39;s possible military family background.  Your husband could have some good insights into BTK from that perspective. <BR> <BR>I hope BTK slipped up and used a cereal box that came from somewhere far away - like where he&#39;s been hiding for 20 years &#40;assuming that the &#34;out-of-Wichita&#34; theory is good&#41;.  That would be a major clue.  Probably no such luck, but maybe he should worry that there was something  of that nature that he didn&#39;t control.....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5440-->
<!--Post: 5452--><!--Time: 1107126585-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5452"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 3:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Don&#39;t know if it means anything but the Stamp on the latest envelope show caverns at Carlsbad in New Mexico. Wasn&#39;t there some link between Carlsbad and Billy the Kid?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5452-->
<!--Post: 5522--><!--Time: 1107169949-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5522"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->L2829tad<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->L2829tad<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 3:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just a thought..I seem to recall that the Otero <BR>children were having breakfast,getting ready for <BR>school...Could the breakfast have been &#34;PT&#34;..I <BR>think there&#39;s covert,beit want ads,message boards <BR>whatever,communication going on between this JERK <BR>&#34;Calling him BTK only plays his game&#34;and someone. <BR>&#40;LE,FBI,TV,&#41;This seems like a responce to ? &#34;What were the children having for breakfast to prove it&#39;s you&#34; question thrown at JERK by whoever.. <BR>..As I said..Just a thought..... <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5522-->
<!--Post: 5637--><!--Time: 1107229024-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5637"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:blingbling1169@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cawichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cawichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 7:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Let&#39;s not give him too much credit. We can find a lot we need to know about him through the brick. It may come from a neighborhood &#40;his&#41;, a store-who may have him on surevielence&#40;spelling, sorry!&#41; all they would have to do is go to the local home depots &#40;of its a new brick&#41; or other stores to see what kind they carry, look at the inventory for bricks purchased within a certain amount of time and how many were sold per customer. If you only sell 3 to one guy-you know he&#39;s not buliding a damn wall!!!  <BR> <BR>Someones home in Wichita who is missing one from their yard, someone may have seen him tka it and had an altercation or gave it to him a while ago. Or shouldn&#39;t the police be canvassing yards to see where it may have come from? They could just drive around a certain neighborhood &#40;they may have tracked BTK to&#41; and they can just look as they patrol-nothing major or out of the way. It may a missing decoration from the yard.  <BR> <BR>The cereal thing is weird because it could be his or like you guys say, it may be someone elses, either way, I think the brick may end up being better than the cereal box! The clay like someone says can be tested for a lot. If it has been in the ground, they can analyze the brick for different organisms, &#40;especially if it has had contact with water&#41;. Wichita is small, but we can narrow it down to certain parks, lakes, rivers and so on that are found only in certain areas, if this is the case, they can surely narrow it down. Good work guys!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5637-->
<!--Post: 5656--><!--Time: 1107253726-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5656"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 2:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Cawitchitan,I agree that they can test this brick. But that is very costly and time consuming. It is not like CSI wher they have experts in house to do the work in a few hours. Most of it is sent to FBI or where ever else for testing. I think that the focus is on physical evidence. Hair, blood, prints, fibers ect. In the mean time the brick may be the back up if nothing else is found.Just a thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5656-->
<!--Post: 5671--><!--Time: 1107275938-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5671"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lorenap<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lorenap<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 8:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He probably just picked it up off the ground in the area. There&#39;s a lot of crap laying around out there. I saw the interview with Ridgeway Friday night on Dateline. He posed one of his victims with two fish some sausage and something else I can&#39;t remember. They were&#39;nt sure if it was his because it was totally off from his m.o. They asked him in the interview if the posing has any special meaning. He said no that they were just some things he had lying around the house and used them to throw police off. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5671-->
<!--Post: 5681--><!--Time: 1107284423-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5681"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 11:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The production code can&#39;t tell where the box was bought..BTK isn&#39;t stupid..there won&#39;t be any fingerprints on it and yes he probaby took it out of someone else&#39;s trashand the brick he found somewhere and used it to throw the police and amateur criminologists like us off the track, so only the contents should be of any real interests...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5681-->
<!--Post: 5713--><!--Time: 1107299902-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5713"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lubbock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lubbock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 3:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Angry: <BR> <BR>Intelligent people make mistakes also. Within the past year theorhetical physicist Stephen Hawking admitted that for decades he&#39;d been wrong that the universe will at some point stop expanding and begin to contract. He now believes it will continue expanding forever. Just an example. I&#39;m sure that BTK isn&#39;t immune to the occasional brain fart - the trick lies in sniffing it out &#40;if you&#39;ll pardon the metaphor&#41;. <BR> <BR>And, KAKE be damned, I still don&#39;t believe that Post distribution centers don&#39;t record what lot #s are loaded on what trucks and bound for where. The same can be said for the truck drivers - what, they don&#39;t carry itemized invoices? Maybe I&#39;m way off, but then again maybe BTK is out there reading this and sweating. <BR> <BR>Another thing. I&#39;m wondering if WPD couldn&#39;t take the box around to different places and run it past the scanners - could they dredge up a record if that particular box was purchased at that particular store, and if so, when? I realize that in a city the size of Wichita this would be a daunting task to say the least, but if WPD does have suspects maybe they could start in their neighborhoods. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5713-->
<!--Post: 5740--><!--Time: 1107315423-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5740"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 7:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I supercopied this link from one of the other threads.  It had good pix of the cereal box, etc. <BR> <BR>Also -- is there any discussion as to what those &#34;streamers&#34; mean?   <BR> <BR>My apology if this was discussed somewhere else. <BR> <BR><a href="http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages?msg=1038.1160" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages?msg=103 8.1160</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5740-->
<!--Post: 5742--><!--Time: 1107316451-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5742"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Woody<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Woody<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 7:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Any barcode experts here?  I know this may sound stupid, but my wife &amp; I use the self-checkout at Wal-Mart all of the time.  Wouldn&#39;t there be a way to tie specific codes to specific transactions &#40;i.e., credit cards, checks, etc.&#41;? <BR> <BR>Go easy on me--I&#39;m a salesman, not a barcode expert.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5742-->
<!--Post: 5780--><!--Time: 1107367669-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5780"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 10:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Woody, <BR> <BR>My guess to your question would be &#34;yes.&#34;  <BR> <BR>I believe they can tie the specific &#40;cereal&#41; item to a credit card or check. <BR> <BR>However, BTK could have used cash, or he may have simply retrieved this box from &#34;garbage.&#34;   <BR> <BR>If he used cash, then an exhaustive review of store surveillance tapes would have to be done.  But the question is &#34;WHICH STORE?&#34;  Also, how long are surveillance tapes kept in archives? <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know if the barcodes can reflect say a &#34;region&#34; where the warehouses stock and deliver to the stores. &#40;That may be somewhat helpful.&#41;  <BR> <BR>My grocery store actually furnishes me coupons based upon my buying patterns.  They call it a customer consumer card &#40;or the like&#41;; but actually they are tracking what you buy and how often. <BR> <BR>I get all kinds of coupons for cat food &amp; treats &#40;printed out right at the register&#41;.  How do they do that?  They know I&#39;ve purchased cat-related items in the past.  I&#39;ve even received a coupon for &#34;pet insurance&#34;! <BR> <BR>I THINK they also use the bar code items to help re-stock inventory and see what is selling &#40;or not&#41;. <BR> <BR>Lots of people buy cereal.  I think even LESS people buy red streamers! <BR> <BR>I&#39;d like to know where the red streamers were purchased!!!  I don&#39;t think BTK happened upon red streamers so easily from trash. <BR> <BR>I think that red streamers are a more distinct purchase &#40;or distinct item&#41;. <BR> <BR>He could have purchased them, or he probably took it from somebody&#39;s existing &#34;personal party inventory.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5780-->
<!--Post: 5801--><!--Time: 1107384945-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5801"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:blingbling1169@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cawichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cawichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 2:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, Nugzter, this is a huge job, but given the length of time he has eluded capture and the fact the the help of the F.B.I. has already been enlisted, they can certainly take care of this. The only chance we have to catch this killer really is him either turning himself in &#40;not gonna happen&#41; or him slipping up somehow. If he leaves us this &#34;evidence&#34; all we can do is take the time to properly analyze it in hopes of finding something helpful. The F.B.I. is not above taking a closer look at the brick if they believe it may prove to be helpful. I am 22 year old student studying Forensic Psychology and I love this stuff. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5801-->
<!--Post: 5813--><!--Time: 1107390373-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5813"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 4:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop -- I think you&#39;re very intelligent.  We may not agree on everything, but that does not cause me to waver when it comes to your intelligence.  When it&#39;s all said and done, I believe people learn that the cereal box is extremely old &#40;maybe even taken from a crime scene&#41;!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5813-->
<!--Post: 5820--><!--Time: 1107391130-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5820"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 4:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The ceral box is brand new.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5820-->
<!--Post: 5840--><!--Time: 1107400298-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5840"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 7:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As for the barcode, Its either the same throught the country OR different per region OR different per retail outlet.  ie Walmart may have a different code than Kmart etc. Im guessing that if its different, where it came from can be determined. Im still wondering about production numbers. Certainly where/when  it was shipped can be determined. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5840-->
<!--Post: 5852--><!--Time: 1107404567-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5852"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Moondog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Moondog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 8:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->For the most part a UPC, or universal price code, is static for a particular product and does not vary by customer.  When Post registered Toasties with the UPC folks they most likely received a single 12-digit code for each package size &#40;i.e. a single UPC they would print on EVERY 12 oz. Toasties box and a different UPC they would print on EVERY 18 oz. box&#41;.  The 18 oz. box of Toasties you purchase at the local grocery store should have the exact same UPC as the 18 oz. box of Toasties you purchase at Target.  The only exception here might be Wal Mart, as they are notorious for pressuring suppliers into offering them exclusive deals - say a 17 oz. box of Toasties. Wal Mart will then sell this 17 oz. box at 10 cents less than Target&#39;s 18 oz. box and thereby give the consumer a false impression that Wal Mart is always cheaper.  If the box is an odd-ball size exclusive to Wal Mart then it&#39;s source can be narrowed down, though there are thousands of Wal Mart stores. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5852-->
<!--Post: 5858--><!--Time: 1107405646-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5858"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Moondog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Moondog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 8:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The most valuable piece of information &#40;other than fingerprints&#41; LE will obtain from the Toasties box is the lot#/date code.  Food manufacturers assign lot codes to each run or batch they make for tracing purposes.  My fiancee &amp; I both work for a large food ingredient supplier and she is involved with our company&#39;s food safety program.  We routinely perform &#39;mock recalls&#39; which entail a fabricated customer complaint - &#34;we&#39;ve found large metal shavings in your product&#34; for example.  It is our responsibility to immediately act upon such a complaint by determining which lot number&#40;s&#41; were shipped to the complaining customer and then examining production, quality analysis, and sales information for the particular batch or batches in question.  The goal is to pinpoint the exact location of every single box or bag of that particluar lot within one hour of the complaint and notify any and all customers who purchased the lot of the possible danger to the public and recall any final product which ended up on store shelves.  So the answer to the general question is &#39;yes&#39; - the box is valuable to the investigation.  LE should be able to provide Post with the lot#/date code and find out where each and every box of that particular batch was shipped.  Post Toasties is not a very popular cereal so this may not be &#39;the needle in the haystack&#39; is seems.  Sorry for the book - this is one of the few areas I may actually be of help.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5858-->
<!--Post: 5902--><!--Time: 1107450259-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5902"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 9:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno -- why are you so certain that the cereal box is brand-new?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5902-->
<!--Post: 5964--><!--Time: 1107467912-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5964"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:blingbling1169@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Cawichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cawichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 1:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lmuncy, it is common knowledge now that the box is one of the most recent and available on the market now. Everyone is sure the box is new, we just want to know where it comes from!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5964-->
<!--Post: 5975--><!--Time: 1107471354-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5975"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 2:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kraft Foods Inc. and their parent company Altria have been involved in a series of restructuring actions and new product initiatives. The Post Healty Classics ® brand with the heart on the box of the Post line of cereals was launched within the last couple of years, I believe in 2003. This Post Toasties box in question is probably no more that an few months old.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5975-->
<!--Post: 6227--><!--Time: 1107605127-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6227"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 4:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Cawichitan, thats awesome. What kind of info do you think they can get from the box. Fibers, hair, prints. They probably have all that on him anyway. Your right. Why a brick? The only reason I can come up with is weight. Now tracking the brick is got to be hard. How do they testa brick? Help me understand.. Cool<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6227-->
